findings.evidence:
```java
resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE, groupResource -> {
    if (hasPermission(groupResource.getId(), VIEW_MEMBERS, MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
        granted.add(groupResource.getId());  // ❌ adds resource UUID
    }
});
```

findings.suggestion:
```java
resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE, groupResource -> {
    // Skip type-level resource (name equals the type string)
    if (groupResource.getName().equals(AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE)) {
        return;
    }
    if (hasPermission(groupResource.getName(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
        granted.add(groupResource.getName());  // ✅ group ID (resource name = group.getId())
    }
});
```

Replace `groupResource.getId()` with `groupResource.getName()` on line 123. The resource name is set to `group.getId()` by `AdminPermissionsSchema.resolveGroup` (line 185) and `resourceStore.create(resourceServer, name, ...)` (line 121), so `groupResource.getName()` returns the group ID that downstream consumers expect:

```java
resourceStore.findByType(server, AdminPermissionsSchema.GROUPS_RESOURCE_TYPE, groupResource -> {
    if (hasPermission(groupResource.getName(), AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW_MEMBERS, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE_MEMBERS)) {
        granted.add(groupResource.getName());
    }
});
```

Note: line 122 has the same bug (passing `groupResource.getId()` to `hasPermission` instead of `groupResource.getName()`) — see the related finding. Both lines should use `groupResource.getName()`.
